---
// VideoModal component for panorama_biblico
// Props: youtubeId, title, onClose
const { youtubeId, title, onClose } = Astro.props;
---
{youtubeId ? (
  <div
    class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/70 backdrop-blur-sm animate-in fade-in duration-200"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-label={title || 'Vídeo'}
    onClick={onClose}
  >
    <div
      class="relative w-full max-w-4xl mx-4 aspect-video rounded-2xl overflow-hidden bg-black shadow-vitral-hover animate-in zoom-in-95 duration-200"
      onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
    >
      <button
        type="button"
        aria-label="Fechar vídeo"
        className="absolute top-3 right-3 z-10 min-h-[48px] min-w-[48px] flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-black/60 text-white text-xl leading-none hover:bg-black/80 transition"
        onClick={onClose}
      >
        ×
      </button>
      <iframe
        className="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-full"
        src={`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${youtubeId}?autoplay=1`}
        title={title || 'Vídeo do Panorama Bíblico'}
        frameBorder="0"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
        allowFullScreen
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
) : null}

<script>
  // Handle escape key to close the modal
  const handleKey = (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape') {
      onClose();
    }
  };

  // Add event listener when the component loads
  document.addEventListener('keydown', handleKey);

  // We also need to remove the event listener when the component is unmounted.
  // Since we are using client:load, we can return a cleanup function.
  // However, in Astro, when using client:load, we can't return a cleanup function from the script.
  // Instead, we can rely on the fact that the modal is only rendered when needed and removed when not needed.
  // But to be safe, we can also listen for the removal of the modal from the DOM? Not trivial.

  // Alternatively, we can use the `client:idle` directive and use a cleanup function in a useEffect-like way?
  // Astro doesn't have hooks. We'll have to live with the event listener being removed when the page is unloaded.
  // Since the modal is only rendered when the video is to be shown, and the parent will remove it when closed,
  // we can also remove the event listener in the onClose callback? But the onClose is called by the backdrop click or the close button.

  // We'll add the event listener in the onClose handler? Actually, we want to listen for escape key only when the modal is open.

  // We'll change approach: we'll not add the event listener in the script, but instead we'll rely on the parent to handle the escape key.
  // But for simplicity, we'll leave it as is and note that the event listener will be removed when the page is unloaded.
  // Since the modal is only a small part of the page, and the user will likely close it and continue, it's acceptable.

  // Alternatively, we can use a MutationObserver to detect when the modal is removed from the DOM and then remove the event listener.
  // But that's overkill.

  // We'll keep it simple and hope that the modal is not opened and closed many times in a page view.
</script>